[b]QLC+ Swiss Knife v1.6.0 — looks and chasers by palette and pattern[/b]

A new release of Swiss Knife, the free companion toolkit for QLC+ 5 workspaces (not affiliated with the QLC+ project).

[list]
[*][b]Looks[/b] — tick fixture groups and palette colours (warm, cold, scenic or your own): one scene per group × colour. The colour is set by what each fixture can do (RGB/RGBW mixing, colour wheel or dimmer), and every channel is declared, so no LTP leftovers.
[*][b]Chasers[/b] — all-hit, left/right, chase, ping-pong, build-up or seeded random across a fixture group; step time in ms or BPM + note length; cut or fade; background colour for the fixtures that are off.
[*][b]Song presets[/b] — save a chaser recipe by name and reuse it.
[*][b]Preview[/b] — each fixture's colour per step, decoded from the DMX values that will be written, with Play.
[*]Optional VC page with coloured buttons; names follow your naming profile; the Workspace Doctor checks the result.
[/list]

Your original show file is never changed — every result is a new _v<N+1>.qxw.

Download: [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/releases/tag/v1.6.0]GitHub release v1.6.0[/url] · [url=https://github.com/giopas/qlc-plus-swiss-knife-tool-script/wiki]Wiki[/url]
